From Zoom Conversations to Golden Knowledge: Turning SDLC Discussions into Reusable Enterprise Intelligence

How Microsoft 365, SharePoint, Microsoft Stream, AI Agents and GAIP can transform everyday engineering conversations into structured, trusted and reusable knowledge

Every organization has an enormous amount of valuable knowledge that never makes it into a formal document.

It lives in:

Requirement discussions

Technical design forums

Architecture reviews

Backlog grooming sessions

Development discussions

Testing and defect reviews

UAT discussions

Product-owner walkthroughs

Production incident reviews

Lessons-learned sessions


At HSBC, many of these conversations happen through Zoom.

A typical one-hour discussion can contain decisions that took months of experience to arrive at:

> Why was this design selected?



> Why does this process have this validation?



> What happens when a Trade Loan crosses a particular threshold?



> Why was an API designed in a particular way?



> What business rule caused this test case?



> Why was a particular exception introduced?



Unfortunately, after the meeting ends, much of this knowledge remains trapped inside a recording or transcript.

The opportunity is therefore not simply to "build another RAG system."

The opportunity is to create a Knowledge Engineering Pipeline that converts conversations into structured, reusable, governed enterprise knowledge.


