14. Why the knowledge graph matters

A vector database is excellent at finding semantically similar text.

A knowledge graph can explicitly represent:

> Customer → submits → Documents



> Documents → enable → Credit Limit Validation



> Credit Validation → precedes → Sanctions Screening



> Sanctions Screening → required before → Loan Approval



This creates a richer representation of enterprise knowledge.

It also provides a foundation for future use cases such as:

impact analysis

dependency analysis

traceability

